[Event "Positional repertoire"]
[Side "black"]
[Style "positional"]
[Name "Caro-Kann Defence"]
[Summary "A rock-solid answer to 1.e4: support ...d5 with ...c6, develop your bishop outside the pawn chain, and never get blown off the board."]
[Result "*"]

1. e4
1... c6 { Prepare ...d5 so you can challenge e4 with a pawn that is already supported. [%cal Gc6d5] }
2. d4
( 2. Nc3 { [%dev] White develops first. }
  2... d5 { Challenge e4. [%cal Gd5e4] }
  3. Nf3
  3... Bg4 { Pin the knight and get the bishop out before ...e6. [%cal Gg4f3] }
  4. h3
  4... Bxf3 { Trade so you keep a healthy pawn structure. }
  5. Qxf3
  5... e6 { Solid. Next ...Nf6, ...Be7 and castle. [%cal Bg8f6] } )
( 2. d3 { [%dev] A quiet King's Indian setup. }
  2... d5 { Take the centre. }
  3. Nd2
  3... e5 { Grab a full share of the centre. [%cal Ge5d4] }
  4. Ngf3
  4... Bd6 { Guard e5 and prepare to castle. }
  5. g3
  5... Nf6 { Develop; castle next. }
  6. Bg2
  6... O-O { Your king is safe and your centre is strong. } )
( 2. Nf3 { [%dev] Another developing move. }
  2... d5 { Challenge e4. }
  3. e5
  3... Bf5 { Develop the bishop outside the chain, the Caro-Kann's trademark. [%cal Gf5d3] }
  4. d4
  4... e6 { Solid; next ...c5 hits White's centre. [%cal Bc6c5] } )
( 2. c4 { [%dev] White hits d5 early. }
  2... d5 { Challenge the centre anyway. }
  3. exd5
  3... cxd5
  4. cxd5
  4... Nf6 { Develop and win back the pawn next move. [%cal Gf6d5] }
  5. Nc3
  5... Nxd5 { Recapture with a centralised knight. Next ...Nc6 and ...e6. }
  6. Nf3
  6... Nc6 { Development and pressure on d4. [%cal Gc6d4] } )
( 2. Bc4 { [%dev] The bishop aims at f7. [%cal Rc4f7] }
  2... d5 { Hit the bishop with a pawn. [%cal Gd5c4] }
  3. exd5
  3... cxd5
  4. Bb5+
  4... Nc6 { Block and develop. }
  5. Nf3
  5... Nf6 { Develop. Next ...Bg4 and ...e6; you have a nice centre. [%cal Bc8g4] } )
2... d5 { Challenge e4. [%cal Gd5e4] }
3. Nc3 { White defends e4. [%cal Rc3e4] }
( 3. e5 { The Advance. [%dev] }
  3... Bf5 { Develop the bishop outside the pawn chain before ...e6. [%cal Gf5d3] }
  4. Nf3
  4... e6 { Solid. Next ...c5 hits the base of White's chain. [%cal Bc6c5] }
  5. Be2
  5... c5 { Strike d4. [%cal Gc5d4] }
  6. O-O
  6... Nc6 { Pile up on d4. Then ...Nge7 and ...Ng6. [%cal Gc6d4] } )
( 3. exd5 { The Exchange. [%dev] }
  3... cxd5 { Recapture; the c-file opens for you. [%cal Gc8c1] }
  4. Bd3
  4... Nc6 { Develop and pressure d4. [%cal Gc6d4] }
  5. c3
  5... Nf6 { Develop. }
  6. Bf4
  6... Bg4 { Develop the bishop outside the chain and pin the queen. [%cal Gg4d1] }
  7. Qb3
  7... Qd7 { Guard b7 and connect toward castling. Next ...e6 and ...Bd6. [%cal Gd7b7] } )
